{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8be7180f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.007997,"end_time":"2026-11-25T23:32:08.175493+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T23:32:08.167496+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Numerai Classic v6.0 (\"Unity\") — LightGBM Regressor (`NumeraiExtractions` + `LightGBMNumeraiEstimator`)\n","\n","- **Data Loading (`data_utils.load_unity_numerai_data`)**: Resolves and downloads the Unity v6.0 Parquets using the official Kaggle clients (`kagglehub.dataset_download` and `kaggle.api.kaggle_api_extended.KaggleApi`) with `numerapi.NumerAPI` fallback, catching each library's actual exception classes (`KaggleApiHTTPError`, `UnauthenticatedError`, `CredentialError`, `NotFoundError`, `DataCorruptionError`, `BackendError`, `KaggleEnvironmentError`, `ColabEnvironmentError`, `kaggle.rest.ApiException`, `HTTPError`, `OSError`, `ValueError`).\n","- **Exploratory Data Analysis (`# EDA`)**: Lists available `TARGET_COL` and `feature_set` options from `features.json`, inspects `train_df.head(2)` / `validation_df.head(2)` and `info()`, plots era sizes over time (`groupby(ERA_COL)[TARGET_COL].size()`), overlays feature standard-deviation distributions across Train vs. Validation, and displays the top 10 features correlated with `TARGET_COL` along with ADF stationarity checks.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 1. Feature Extraction Parameters (`utils.NumeraiExtractions` — `estimator__extractor__*`)\n","- **`era_col`** (`[ERA_COL]`): Column name containing the sequential weekly time index (`'era'`).\n","- **`ticker_col`** (`[TICKER_COL]`): Column name containing the security identifier (`'numerai_ticker'`).\n","- **`target_col`** (`[TARGET_COL, 'target_cyrusd_20', 'target_teager2b_20']`): Target column used when ranking features by target correlation.\n","- **`year_horizon_filter`** (`[None, (1, 2, 3), (4, 5, 6), (7, 8, 9)]`): Restricts `fit()` variance and correlation estimation to specific 52-week training year buckets `(era - 1) // 52 + 1` (`None` uses all training years; never exposed as a model feature).\n","- **`variance_threshold`** (`[None, 0.02, 0.05, 0.10]`): Drops near-constant features whose training variance is $\\le$ threshold via `sklearn.feature_selection.VarianceThreshold` (`None` keeps all features).\n","- **`correlation_method`** (`[None, 'pandas_mean', 'numerai_mean', 'pearson', 'spearman']`):\n","  - `None`: Skips correlation ranking and keeps original column order.\n","  - `'pandas_mean'`: Computes per-era Pearson correlation (`era_df.corrwith(era_target)`) and averages across eras.\n","  - `'numerai_mean'`: Computes official per-era `numerai_tools.scoring.numerai_corr` and averages across eras.\n","  - `'pearson'`: Global pooled Pearson correlation (`r_regression`) across all rows.\n","  - `'spearman'`: Global pooled Spearman rank correlation across all rows.\n","- **`abs_corr`** (`[True, False]`): `True` ranks features by $|\\text{corr}|$ (strongest magnitude in either direction); `False` ranks by signed $\\text{corr}$ (positive only first).\n","- **`top_k`** (`[None, 10, 20, 40]`): Keeps only the top $K$ highest-ranked features from the extractor (`None` keeps all features).\n","- **`feature_selection_percentile`** (`[None, 25.0, 50.0, 75.0, 100.0]`): Keeps the top percentage of ranked features (`None` keeps all features).\n","- **`sparse_selector`** (`[None, 'lasso', 'elasticnet']`) & **`sparse_alpha`** (`[0.001, 0.01, 0.1]` / `Real(1e-4, 1e-1, prior='log-uniform')`): Optional multivariate sparse feature selection via `sklearn.feature_selection.SelectFromModel` with `Lasso` or `ElasticNet` fitted strictly inside `fit()` (`None` disables).\n","- **`pca_n_components`** (`[None, 10, 20, 40]` / `0.90`): Optional `sklearn.decomposition.PCA` compression fitted strictly inside `fit()` and quantized to `0..4` `int8` bins in `transform()` to reduce feature exposure without dropping features (`None` disables).\n","- **`quantize_scope`** (`['era', 'train_fit', 'global']`) & **`quantize_strategy`** (`['zscore', 'quantile']`): Controls how continuous derived features are quantized into `0..4` `int8` bins (`'era'` = leak-free within-era cross-sectional quantization; `'train_fit'` = frozen `StandardScaler` fitted strictly on training data in `fit()`; `'global'` = legacy full-array quantization; `'zscore'` = z-score rounding vs. `'quantile'` = `KBinsDiscretizer` quantile edges).\n","- **`sequence_top_n`** (`[4, 2, 8]`): Number of top-ranked features expanded by rolling-era, lag-diff, and per-ticker sequence extractors.\n","- **`missing_fill_value`** (`[2.0, 0.0, 4.0, 'mean', 'median', 'era_mean', 'era_median']`):\n","  - `2.0`, `0.0`, `4.0`, `'mean'`, `'median'`: Imputes missing values via `sklearn.impute.SimpleImputer` (`2.0` is the neutral middle bin of Numerai's `0..4` scale).\n","  - `'era_mean'` / `'era_median'`: Fills missing values with each feature's within-era cross-sectional mean or median.\n","- **`feature_groups`** (`unity_feature_groups` on `NumeraiExtractions`, `None` if no thematic groups exist in `feature_metadata['feature_sets']`; omitted from CV search spaces to prevent console log bloat) & **`basic_group_stats`** (`[None, 'mean', 'std', 'skew', 'mean|std', 'mean|skew', 'std|skew', 'mean|std|skew']`): Computes leak-free row-wise summary statistics (`mean`, `std`, `skew` quantized to `0..4` bins) across real Unity v6.0 feature groups or built-in thematic prefixes (`None` disables).\n","- **`fourier_period_eras`** (`[52, 26, 13]`): Cycle length in eras (52 = annual, 26 = semi-annual, 13 = quarterly) used by `fourier_order`.\n","- **`fourier_order`** (`[None, 1, 2, 3]`): Sole cyclical seasonality encoding — adds smooth $\\sin(2\\pi k \\cdot \\text{era} / P)$ and $\\cos(2\\pi k \\cdot \\text{era} / P)$ harmonics for $k=1..\\text{fourier\\_order}$ quantized to `0..4` bins (`None` disables).\n","- **`include_rolling_era`** (`[False, True]`) & **`rolling_era_windows`** (`[(4, 12), (2, 6, 12), (4, 8, 16)]`): When `include_rolling_era=True`, computes causal rolling era means over each window length $W$ in `rolling_era_windows` for the top correlated features, quantized to `0..4` bins.\n","- **`include_lag_diff`** (`[False, True]`) & **`era_lag_scales`** (`[(1, 2, 4), (1, 2, 4, 8), (2, 4, 8)]`): When `include_lag_diff=True`, computes causal era-to-era lag differences ($\\bar{x}_e - \\bar{x}_{e-k}$) for each lag step $k$ in `era_lag_scales`, quantized to `0..4` bins.\n","- **`ticker_features`** (`[None, 'rolling_mean', 'momentum_diff', 'weeks_since_high', 'rolling_rank', 'weeks_since_change', 'expanding_stats', 'raw_lags', 'rolling_mean|momentum_diff', 'rolling_mean|momentum_diff|rolling_rank', 'expanding_stats|raw_lags', 'rolling_mean|momentum_diff|weeks_since_high|rolling_rank|weeks_since_change|expanding_stats|raw_lags']`), **`ticker_windows`** (`[(4, 12), (2, 6, 12)]`), & **`ticker_lag_steps`** (`[None, (1, 2), (1, 2, 4)]`): Computes causal per-ticker time-series features grouped strictly by `numerai_ticker` sorted chronologically by `era` (`None` disables).\n","- **`era_dispersion_features`** (`[None, 'mean', 'std', 'extreme_frac', 'mean|std', 'mean|extreme_frac', 'std|extreme_frac', 'mean|std|extreme_frac']`): Adds per-row cross-sectional mean (`'mean'`), standard deviation (`'std'`), and fraction of extreme `0`/`4` bins (`'extreme_frac'`) across selected features (`None` disables).\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 2. Shared Parent Estimator Parameters (`baseline_utils.BaseNumeraiEstimator` — `estimator__*`)\n","- **`correlation_method`** (`[None, 'pandas_mean', 'numerai_mean', 'pearson', 'spearman']`): How the estimator scores post-extraction features against `TARGET_COL` (used when `top_k` is set).\n","- **`abs_corr`** (`[True, False]`): `True` selects top features by $|\\text{corr}|$; `False` selects by signed $\\text{corr}$.\n","- **`top_k`** (`[None, 20, 40, 80]`): Number of top post-extraction features passed to LightGBM (`None` uses all extracted features).\n","- **`era_weighting`** (`[None, 'equal_era', 'recency_linear', 'recency_exp']`): Computes per-row `sample_weight` passed into `LGBMRegressor.fit(...)` (`None`, equal weight per era, linear recency, or exponential recency decay).\n","- **`recency_decay`** (`Real(0.001, 0.020)`): Exponential decay rate per era when `era_weighting='recency_exp'`.\n","- **`prediction_transform`** (`[None, 'era_zscore', 'era_rank']`): Post-prediction within-era normalization (`None` = raw, `'era_zscore'`, or `'era_rank'`).\n","- **`bias_correction`** (`[None, 'mean_residual']`): When `'mean_residual'`, records `mean(y_train - y_hat_train)` in `fit()` and adds it to predictions in `predict()` (`None` disables).\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 3. LightGBM Model Parameters (`lgbm_utils.LightGBMNumeraiEstimator` — `estimator__*`)\n","- **Boosting & Objective**:\n","  - **`boosting_type`** (`['gbdt', 'dart', 'rf']`): Gradient boosting decision trees, Dropouts meet Multiple Additive Regression Trees, or Random Forest.\n","  - **`objective`** (`['regression', 'regression_l1', 'huber', 'fair', 'quantile']`): Loss function (`'regression'` = L2/MSE, `'regression_l1'` = L1/MAE, `'huber'`, `'fair'`, `'quantile'`).\n","  - **`alpha`** (`[0.9, 0.5, 1.0]` / `Real(0.1, 2.0)`): Huber loss delta or Quantile loss $\\alpha$ when `objective` is `'huber'` or `'quantile'`.\n","  - **`fair_c`** (`[1.0, 0.5, 2.0]` / `Real(0.1, 5.0)`): Scale parameter $c$ when `objective='fair'`.\n","- **Tree Structure & Learning Schedule**:\n","  - **`n_estimators`** (`[200, 100, 500, 1000, 2000]` / `Integer(50, 2000)`): Number of boosting rounds (trees).\n","  - **`learning_rate`** (`[0.05, 0.01, 0.03, 0.1]` / `Real(0.005, 0.15, prior='log-uniform')`): Shrinkage rate per boosting iteration.\n","  - **`num_leaves`** (`[31, 15, 63, 127]` / `Integer(7, 128)`): Maximum tree leaves for base learners (auto-clamped to $2^{\\text{max\\_depth}}$ when `max_depth > 0`).\n","  - **`max_depth`** (`[5, -1, 3, 4, 6, 8]` / `Integer(2, 10)`): Maximum tree depth (`-1` = unlimited).\n","  - **`extra_trees`** (`[False, True]`): Extremely randomized threshold selection per feature to reduce overfitting.\n","  - **`linear_tree`** (`[False, True]`) & **`linear_lambda`** (`[0.0, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0]` / `Real(0.0, 5.0)`): Fits piecewise linear models at tree leaves with L2 penalty `linear_lambda`.\n","- **Leaf Constraints & Regularization**:\n","  - **`min_split_gain`** (`[0.0, 0.001, 0.01, 0.1]` / `Real(0.0, 0.5)`): Minimum loss reduction required to make a split.\n","  - **`min_child_weight`** (`[1e-3, 1e-2, 1.0, 10.0]` / `Real(1e-4, 10.0, prior='log-uniform')`): Minimum sum of instance hessian in a leaf.\n","  - **`min_child_samples`** (`[20, 50, 100, 200]` / `Integer(10, 300)`): Minimum number of rows needed in a leaf (`min_data_in_leaf`).\n","  - **`reg_alpha`** (`[0.0, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0]` / `Real(0.0, 10.0)`): L1 regularization term on leaf weights.\n","  - **`reg_lambda`** (`[0.0, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0]` / `Real(0.0, 10.0)`): L2 regularization term on leaf weights.\n","  - **`path_smooth`** (`[0.0, 1.0, 10.0, 50.0]` / `Real(0.0, 50.0)`): Hierarchical leaf smoothing toward parent node predictions.\n","  - **`max_delta_step`** (`[0.0, 0.5, 1.0]` / `Real(0.0, 2.0)`): Limits maximum leaf output magnitude (`0.0` = no constraint).\n","- **Subsampling & Feature Fraction**:\n","  - **`subsample`** (`[1.0, 0.8, 0.6]` / `Real(0.5, 1.0)`): Row bagging fraction (`bagging_fraction`).\n","  - **`subsample_freq`** (`[0, 1, 5]` / `Integer(0, 5)`): Frequency of row bagging (`0` disables; auto-enforced $\\ge 1$ for `boosting_type='rf'`).\n","  - **`colsample_bytree`** (`[0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 0.8, 1.0]` / `Real(0.05, 1.0)`): Fraction of features randomly chosen per tree (`feature_fraction`).\n","  - **`colsample_bynode`** (`[1.0, 0.5, 0.8]` / `Real(0.3, 1.0)`): Fraction of features randomly chosen at each split node (`feature_fraction_bynode`).\n","- **Histogram Binning**:\n","  - **`max_bin`** (`[255, 5, 15, 63]` / `Categorical([5, 15, 63, 255])`): Maximum number of bins for feature bucketing (`5` matches Numerai's native `0..4` int8 bins).\n","  - **`min_data_in_bin`** (`[3, 5, 10]` / `Integer(1, 20)`): Minimum number of rows inside one histogram bin.\n","  - **`subsample_for_bin`** (`[200000, 50000, 500000]`): Number of samples used to construct histogram bins.\n","- **DART Parameters** (active when `boosting_type='dart'`):\n","  - **`drop_rate`** (`[0.1, 0.05, 0.2]` / `Real(0.01, 0.3)`), **`max_drop`** (`[50, 20, 100]` / `Integer(10, 100)`), **`skip_drop`** (`[0.5, 0.3, 0.7]` / `Real(0.1, 0.9)`), **`xgboost_dart_mode`** (`[False, True]`), **`uniform_drop`** (`[False, True]`).\n","- **System & Diagnostics**:\n","  - **`importance_type`** (`['gain', 'split']`), **`feature_pre_filter`** (`[True, False]`), **`force_col_wise`** (`[False, True]`), **`force_row_wise`** (`[False, True]`), **`n_jobs`** (`[lgbm_n_jobs]`), **`lgbm_verbosity`** (`[-1]`).\n","\n","---\n","\n","- **Evaluation (`utils.evaluate_numerai_predictions`)**: Reports official `numerai_tools.scoring.numerai_corr`, per-era `Spearman Correlation`, `Average Payout` (`(corrs / 0.2).clip(-1, 1)`), `Sharpe Ratio` (`corrs.mean() / corrs.std()`), `Mean Absolute Error (MAE)`, `Forecast Bias` (`mean(y_true - y_pred)`), `Directional Hit Rate` (sign agreement vs. `0.5`), `Era CORR Lag-1 ACF`, `Ljung-Box p-value` (`acorr_ljungbox`), `ARCH-LM p-value` (`het_arch`), `ADF Stationarity p-value` (`adfuller`), `Skewness`, `Excess Kurtosis`, `Jarque-Bera p-value`, `Max Drawdown`, and validation `Feature Exposure`."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"f5829202","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T23:32:08.194887Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T23:32:08.194568Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T23:32:24.446732Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T23:32:24.445651Z"},"papermill":{"duration":16.262536,"end_time":"2026-11-25T23:32:24.448962+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T23:32:08.186426+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs